[I] EFI Unified Kernel Image Maker

[T] efi-mkuki is a simple POSIX shell script for creating an EFI Unified
[T] Kernel Image, a single EFI PE executable combining an EFI stub loader,
[T] the kernel, its command line and optionally an initramfs, CPU microcode
[T] and a splash image. Such an image boots Linux directly from UEFI and can
[T] easily be signed for Secure Boot.

[U] https://github.com/jirutka/efi-mkuki

[A] Efi-mkuki Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

